            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic flexor carpi radialis brevis: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>633-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jhsa.2009.12.028</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a flexor carpi radialis brevis (FCRB) is reported. In contrast to all but one previous case, the anomalous FCRB was painful. The FCRB tendon was located in a separate compartment; the tenosynovitis in that compartment was the likely cause of pain. Release of the compartment relieved the symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
